\appendix
\section{GRMHD Eigenstructure and Characteristic Wave Speeds}

In this appendix we summarize the one-dimensional GRMHD eigenstructure used
to construct HLLE-type numerical fluxes and CFL stability bounds in SMSE-v1.
We consider a single spatial direction $x$ with metric components
$g_{\mu\nu}$ and a fluid state $(\rho, p, v^x, B^x)$.

\subsection{Primitive and Conserved Variables}

The primitive variables are
\begin{equation}
P = (\rho, p, v^x, B^x),
\end{equation}
and the conserved variables in $3+1$ form are
\begin{equation}
U = (D, S_x, \tau, B^x),
\end{equation}
where
\begin{align}
D   &= \rho W,\\
S_x &= (\rho h + b^2) W^2 v^x - b^0 b^x,\\
\tau &= (\rho h + b^2) W^2 - \left(p + \frac{b^2}{2}\right) - D.
\end{align}
Here $W$ is the Lorentz factor and $b^\mu$ the magnetic 4-vector.

\subsection{Sound Speed and Alfv\'en Speed}

For an ideal equation of state with adiabatic index $\Gamma$, the sound speed
is
\begin{equation}
c_s^2 = \frac{\Gamma p}{\rho h},
\end{equation}
and the Alfv\'en speed in the fluid frame is
\begin{equation}
v_A^2 = \frac{b^2}{\rho h + b^2},
\end{equation}
where $b^2 = b_\mu b^\mu$.

\subsection{Fast Magnetosonic Speed}

The fast magnetosonic speed $v_{\mathrm{ms}}$ is given by
\begin{equation}
v_{\mathrm{ms}}^2
=
\frac{1}{2}
\left[
c_s^2 + v_A^2
+
\sqrt{(c_s^2 + v_A^2)^2 - 4 c_s^2 v_A^2}
\right].
\end{equation}
This speed sets the dominant characteristic wave bound for GRMHD fluxes.

\subsection{Characteristic Eigenvalues in 3+1 Form}

In the $3+1$ ADM decomposition, the coordinate-frame characteristic speeds
along $x$ are
\begin{equation}
\lambda_{\pm}
=
\frac{\alpha}{1 - v^x \beta^x}
\left(
v^x \pm v_{\mathrm{ms}}
\right)
-
\beta^x,
\end{equation}
where $\alpha$ is the lapse and $\beta^x$ the shift component.

For HLLE fluxes, we define
\begin{align}
a_L &= \min\left(\lambda_{\mathrm{min}}^{L}, \lambda_{\mathrm{min}}^{R}\right),\\
a_R &= \max\left(\lambda_{\mathrm{max}}^{L}, \lambda_{\mathrm{max}}^{R}\right),
\end{align}
where the superscripts $L$ and $R$ denote left and right states at an
interface.

\subsection{CFL Stability Condition}

The relativistic CFL time-step bound in SMSE-v1 is
\begin{equation}
\Delta t
\le
\mathcal{C}_{\mathrm{CFL}}
\left[
\max_i
\left(
\frac{
|\lambda_{+,i}| + |\lambda_{-,i}|
}{
\Delta x^i
}
\right)
\right]^{-1},
\end{equation}
with $\mathcal{C}_{\mathrm{CFL}} \in (0,1)$ a safety factor and $\Delta x^i$
the coordinate cell widths.

This eigenstructure underpins the HLLE flux construction, CFL enforcement,
and stability guarantees of the SMSE-v1 GRMHD solver.